    <entry_item>
      <dico>Lessing</dico>
      <unicode>ᠺᠠᠯᠠᠪ</unicode>
      <transcript>GALAB, ΓALAB</transcript>
      <definition>(fr. S.); T. bskal par bskal dus; S. kalpa. Time with reference to cosmic ages, eon. See Pt.I under γalab and ED 172.</definition>
      <page>1170</page>
      <examples>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠡᠪᠳᠡᠷᠡᠺᠦᠢ ᠺᠠᠯᠠᠪ</unicode>
          <transcript>+++ ebderekyi -- ;</transcript>
          <definition>hjig (pahi) bskal (pa); S. samvartakalpa. Eon of destruction (of the world). ED540a.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠭᠠᠯ ᠤᠨ ᠺᠠᠯᠠᠪ</unicode>
          <transcript>+++ γal un -- ;</transcript>
          <definition>T. mehi bskal pa, mes hjig pa; S. tejahsamvartani. The period during which the universe will be destroyed by fire.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠶᠡᠺᠡ ᠺᠠᠯᠠᠪ</unicode>
          <transcript>+++ jeke --;</transcript>
          <definition>T. bskal par chen po,bskal chen; S. maha -kalpa. The great period, the duration of the world from its begimiing to its destruction.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠰᠠᠶᠢᠨ ᠺᠠᠯᠠᠪ</unicode>
          <transcript>+++ sain --;</transcript>
          <definition>T. bskal bzang po; S. bhadra-kalpa. A good kalpa, a kalpa during which five Bus. Appear successively.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠲᠣᠭᠲᠠᠬᠤᠢ ᠺᠠᠯᠠᠪ</unicode>
          <transcript>+++ toγtaxui -- ;</transcript>
          <definition>T. hchags bskal pa; S. vivarta-kalpa. The period of regeneration.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠬᠣᠭᠤᠰᠤᠨ ᠺᠠᠯᠠᠪ</unicode>
          <transcript>+++ xoγusun -- ;</transcript>
          <definition>T. stong pahi bskal pa; S. çūnya-kalpa. An empty kalpa, an eon in which no Bu. appears.</definition>
        </example>
      </examples>
    </entry_item>
